# taranity.com - environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Everything is optional for local development:
# analytics stays off in `astro dev`. For no-widget contact demo mode, explicitly
# set PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=off while running `astro dev`.
#
# The PUBLIC_ values below are build-time and client-exposed (none are secret).
# The contact form additionally needs two values set as Cloudflare Pages
# environment variables on the deployment, NOT in this file - see the bottom.

# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token (cookieless; PUBLIC, it ships in every
# page's HTML). The production token is hardcoded in src/config/site.ts - leave
# this empty. Set only to override it, or to `off` as a preview/incident kill
# switch (a lasting disable also needs the privacy page + verify-deploy updated).
PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key - renders the bot-check widget on the contact
# form. This public key also has a fallback in src/config/site.ts so direct
# Cloudflare Pages uploads still render Turnstile when local env is empty.
# Set this to `off` only for intentional local/demo no-widget builds. For real
# sends, pair a Cloudflare site key with TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY below. Create or
# rotate keys in the Cloudflare dashboard (Turnstile).
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=

# Canonical site URL (also set in astro.config.mjs `site`).
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://taranity.com

# --- Contact form: set these on the Cloudflare Pages deployment, not here ---
# The /api/contact Pages Function reads them at runtime; without them it fails
# closed (no send). Being server-side, they never reach the client.
#
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY          Turnstile secret, pairs with PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY.
#   WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY          Web3Forms access key (https://web3forms.com, no account)
#                                 that the function submits the message through.
#   TURNSTILE_ALLOWED_HOSTNAMES   Optional comma-separated hostname allowlist for
#                                 token validation; default is taranity.com,
#                                 www.taranity.com, and *.taranity.pages.dev.
#
# Abuse protection beyond Turnstile is a Cloudflare WAF rate-limit rule (dashboard:
# Security > WAF > Rate limiting rules, taranity.com zone): it blocks an IP that POSTs
# /api/contact more than 5 times in 10s. It lives in the Cloudflare dashboard, not in
# this repo, so it is recorded here rather than configured here.
